 these into the general standard equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-(-1))^{2} & =4p(y-(-4)) \\\\ (x+1)^{2} & =4p(y+4).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe are left to find the value of $p.$ We know that the given parabola also passes through the point $(1,-2),$ so we can substitute $x=1$ and $y=-2$ into the standard equation and solve for $p:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x+1)^{2} & =4p(y+4) \\\\ (1+1)^{2} & =4p(-2+4) \\\\ 4 & =8p \\\\ p & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the parabola is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x+1)^{2} & =4p(y+4) \\\\ (x+1)^{2} & =4(\\frac{1}{2})(y+4) \\\\ (x+1)^{2} & =2(y+4).\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534044 true] [17592186275885 1000 #edb/ref 17592186275886 13194139534044 true] [17592186275885 1000 #edb/ref 17592186275887 13194139534044 true] [17592186275885 1000 #edb/ref 17592186275888 13194139534044 true] [17592186275885 1000 #edb/ref 17592186275889 13194139534044 true] [17592186275885 1000 #edb/ref 17592186275890 13194139534044 true] [17592186275885 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534044 true] [17592186275885 1041 "selection" 13194139534044 true] [17592186275885 1104 #edb/ref 17592186275888 13194139534044 true] [17592186275885 1110 #uuid "fc03ab09-fe27-590c-bd85-b5f8d0992319" 13194139534044 true] [17592186275886 1034 "(x+4)^{2}=2(y+1)" 13194139534044 true] [17592186275886 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534044 true] [17592186275886 1111 #uuid "05363ca3-93b9-55bc-8ab7-dda9c11c0fee" 13194139534044 true] [17592186275887 1034 "(x+1)^{2}=4(y+4)" 13194139534044 true] [17592186275887 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534044 true] [17592186275887 1111 #uuid "21f91c6b-2db5-572d-afb6-f86984d26d93" 13194139534044 true] [17592186275888 1034 "(x+1)^{2}=2(y+4)" 13194139534044 true] [17592186275888 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534044 true] [17592186275888 1111 #uuid "fcc946d8-6a13-5497-a02f-189e9847dad8" 13194139534044 true] [17592186275889 1034 "(x+1)^{2}=-4(y+4)" 13194139534044 true] [17592186275889 1103 #edb/ref